/P 110 0 R
/E (8)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
210 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 110 0 R
/E (   The IWSR features a single waste compartment, which is further subdivided into four identical sections. These include designated compartments for metal, plastic, glass, and a mixed category for waste that does not conform to the previous classifications. The introduction of a fourth mixed compartment minimizes the likelihood of misclassification during operation. Ultimately, one of the four compartments is not recycled but is instead directed to a landfill. This represents the most efficient solution we have devised, as further division of the container into additional compartments would have proven inefficient. Such an approach would have substantially increased the costs associated with the USDPM due to the necessity for additional servo drives and materials, while also diminishing the bin's capacity, leading to potential overflow within a week and increasing the risk of malfunction in the sorting mechanism.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
211 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 110 0 R
/E (2.4.3 WASTE CONTAINERS)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
