214 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 110 0 R
/E (2.5.1. CONVEYOR)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
215 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 110 0 R
/E (   The initial iteration of the sorting mechanism was fundamentally distinct from the present design. Upon the entry of waste into the inlet, a laser distance sensor recognizes its presence on the conveyor \(figure 8\). This activation initiates the conveyor, transporting the waste toward a chamber responsible for object type identification. Once processing concludes, five servos positioned beneath adjust to the appropriate location, guaranteeing that the waste is directed to the correct compartment.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
